WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.063
Break-even is a rough count: how many sales cover your week.

00:00:04.063 --> 00:00:05.540
No spreadsheet panic required.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.495
This lesson is about break-even without spreadsheets panic.

00:00:08.495 --> 00:00:11.081
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:11.081 --> 00:00:14.774
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:14.774 --> 00:00:20.314
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:20.314 --> 00:00:24.377
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:24.377 --> 00:00:28.440
Stay practical: compute rough break-even before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:34.101
Take weekly cash you need, divide by contribution per sale after rough unit cost.

00:00:34.101 --> 00:00:36.390
Remember the objective: compute rough break-even.

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:40.587
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:40.587 --> 00:00:45.165
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:45.165 --> 00:00:49.361
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:49.361 --> 00:00:53.939
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:53.939 --> 00:00:56.610
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:58.136
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:58.456 --> 00:01:00.689
Write the break-even number of sales.

00:01:00.689 --> 00:01:02.922
